                   uses the RA_SERVER environment variable.

     RA_SERVER     The secondary default whois server.  If this is unset,
                   wwhhooiiss will use _w_h_o_i_s_._i_a_n_a_._o_r_g.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The wwhhooiiss utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To obtain contact information about an administrator located in the Rus‐
     sian TLD domain "RU", use the --cc option as shown in the following exam‐
     ple, where _C_O_N_T_A_C_T_-_I_D is substituted with the actual contact identifier.

           wwhhooiiss --cc RRUU CCOONNTTAACCTT--IIDD

     (Note: This example is specific to the TLD "RU", but other TLDs can be
     queried by using a similar syntax.)

     The following example demonstrates how to query a whois server using a
     non-standard port, where “query-data” is the query to be sent to
     “whois.example.com” on port “rwhois” (written numerically as 4321).

           wwhhooiiss --hh wwhhooiiss..eexxaammppllee..ccoomm --pp rrwwhhooiiss qquueerryy--ddaattaa

     Some whois servers support complex queries with dash-letter options.  You
     can use the ---- option to separate wwhhooiiss command options from whois server
     query options.  A query containing spaces must be quoted as one argument
     to the wwhhooiiss command.  The following example asks the RIPE whois server
     to return a brief description of its “domain” object type:

           wwhhooiiss --rr ---- ''--tt ddoommaaiinn''

